Subject: [PATCH] =?UTF-8?q?P38:=20pgm=5Fbase=20=E2=80=94=20skip=20ReadPdfB?=
 =?UTF-8?q?rowserInfos=20+=20NotificationsManager::Load=20in=20headless?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Two more GUI-only init calls in PGM_BASE::InitPgm that headless
kicad-cli was paying for:

- ReadPdfBrowserInfos: probes for available PDF viewers so the GUI's
  'Open in PDF viewer' menu items know what to offer.
- NotificationsManager::Load: reads on-disk notification-history
  JSON to populate the notifications panel widget.

Both are unused by kicad-cli. Guard on !aHeadless. GUI apps are
unaffected.
---
 common/pgm_base.cpp | 11 +++++++++--
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/common/pgm_base.cpp b/common/pgm_base.cpp
index da390ff2..fc14ed0b 100644
--- a/common/pgm_base.cpp
+++ b/common/pgm_base.cpp
@@ -490,9 +490,16 @@ bool PGM_BASE::InitPgm( bool aHeadless, bool aIsUnitTest )
 
     loadCommonSettings();
 
-    ReadPdfBrowserInfos();      // needs GetCommonSettings()
+    // ReadPdfBrowserInfos is only useful for the GUI (used to launch a
+    // PDF viewer from the eeschema/pcbnew menus). Skip in headless.
+    if( !aHeadless )
+        ReadPdfBrowserInfos();      // needs GetCommonSettings()
 
-    GetNotificationsManager().Load();
+    // Notifications are strictly GUI (populated into the notifications
+    // panel widget). Load parses the on-disk JSON list every time; skip
+    // the file open + parse in headless.
+    if( !aHeadless )
+        GetNotificationsManager().Load();
 
     // TODO(JE): Remove this if apps are refactored to not assume Prj() always works
     // Need to create a project early for now (it can have an empty path for the moment)
-- 
